# STIG AS24-U1-000940: The account used to run the Apache web server must not have 
# STIG ID: V-214271 (HIGH)

META
    esp_id `apache-as24-u1-000940-service-account-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `apache`
    criticality `critical`

    title `STIG AS24-U1-000940: The account used to run the Apache web server must not have a valid login shell `
    description `The account used to run the Apache web server must not have a valid login shell and password defined.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `apache,stig,disa-stig,combined`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:AS24-U1-000940,NIST-800-53:CM-6`
    control_objective `CM-6`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Apache:localhost:web-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `1`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA Apache STIG guidance for AS24-U1-000940.`

    component_id `comp-apache-web`

    impl_CM_6 `This control is validated by checking the Apache HTTP server configuration against the DISA STIG baseline.`

META_END

DEF
    VAR config_path string `/etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf`

    OBJECT module_check
        module `ssl_module`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE module_loaded
        loaded boolean = true
    STATE_END

    OBJECT httpd_config
        path VAR config_path
    OBJECT_END

    STATE directive_present
        content string contains `User apache`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN apache_module
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF module_loaded
            OBJECT_REF module_check
        CTN_END

        CTN file_content
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF directive_present
            OBJECT_REF httpd_config
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
